    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence of validations and side-effects for **POST /api/owners**, as the code stands. The handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:159-207`).\n\n## Before the method runs\n\n1. **Security authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (line 159). Only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; otherwise `DisableSecurityConfig` skips it. 403 on failure.\n\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (`OwnersApi.java:91`). Validated in field order \u2192 400 on any failure:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(1,10)` (optional)\n   - `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(1,255)` (optional)\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1,255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n   - (`postcode`, `sharesHousehold` \u2014 no constraints here)\n\n*(Note: the `Owner`/`Person` entity's own validation annotations do **not** fire \u2014 the entity is never `@Valid`-bound; equivalent checks run explicitly below.)*\n\n## Inside the method body\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** (162-168) \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before, returns the previously-created owner with **200 OK** and does nothing further.\n\n4. **Address normalization \u2014 MUTATION** (169) \u2014 `normalizeAddress`: strips/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, etc.), and composes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` into `address`.\n\n5. **Required-fields validation** (170) \u2014 `OwnerFieldsValidator`: rejects blank `firstName`/`lastName`/`city`/`telephone` and requires at least one of `addressLine1`/`address`. 400 (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`).\n\n6. **Postcode validation** (171) \u2014 `PostcodeValidator`: if present, must be 4 digits and within the city's region range (NSW/VIC/QLD). 400 (`InvalidPostcodeException`).\n\n7. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (173) \u2014 MapStruct; `id`/`pets` ignored.\n\n8. **Telephone normalization \u2014 MUTATION** (174) \u2014 `TelephoneNormalizer`: strips separators, defaults country code to `+61`, validates length, stores canonical E.164. 400 (`InvalidTelephoneException`).\n\n9. **Email normalization \u2014 MUTATION** (175) \u2014 `EmailNormalizer`: blank\u2192null; else regex-check (400 `InvalidEmailException`), lower-case, then disposable-domain blocklist check (400 `DisposableEmailDomainException`).\n\n10. **Future-registration-date check** (176-179) \u2014 rejects a `registrationDate` after the server date. 400 (`FutureRegistrationDateException`).\n\n11. **Registration-date default + business-day roll \u2014 MUTATION** (180-181) \u2014 defaults to today if omitted, then `BusinessDayResolver` rolls weekends/holidays forward.\n\n12. **Daily-registration-limit check** (182-185) \u2014 `countOwnersRegisteredOn` \u2265 100 \u2192 **429** (`OwnerDailyRegistrationLimitExceededException`).\n\n13. **Bulk-signup flag \u2014 MUTATION** (186) \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if today's count > 80.\n\n14. **City-capacity check** (187-189) \u2014 `countOwnersInCity` \u2265 50 \u2192 **409** (`OwnerCityCapacityExceededException`).\n\n15. **Household-id generation \u2014 MUTATION** (190-192) \u2014 if postcode present, `householdId` = SHA-256(normalized lastName + postcode), 12 hex chars.\n\n16. **Duplicate-identity check** (193-195) \u2014 if any owner matches identity key (`telephone|email|householdId`) \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`).\n\n17. **Household-duplicate check** (196-199) \u2014 if another owner shares the `householdId` and the request did not set `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateHouseholdException`).\n\n18. **Persist \u2014 `saveOwner`** (200), `@Transactional` (`ClinicServiceImpl.java:242-261`), deriving in order before the DB write:\n    - **customerCode** \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, deduplicated with `-<n>` on collision\n    - **namesakeCount** \u2014 count of same first+last name\n    - **membershipNumber** \u2014 `<customerCode>-M<YY>` from registration fiscal year\n    - **householdSize** \u2014 household members + 1\n    - **`ownerRepository.save(owner)`** \u2014 `em.persist`, DB-generated id, `pets` cascade (none on create). No JPA lifecycle callbacks/auditing.\n\n19. **Remember idempotency key** (201) \u2014 stores key \u2192 new owner id (no-op if key blank).\n\n20. **Audit log** (202) \u2014 `OwnerAuditLogger.logCreated`: one INFO line to the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n21. **Build response** (203-206) \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\n## Explicitly absent\nNo password encoding (owners have none), no events, emails, notifications, external calls, or caching. The only route-wide aspect is `CallMonitoringAspect`, which merely times `@Repository` calls (JMX) and has no functional effect."
